          %h2#references References
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"}> Rune Haugseng
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher categories
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.14311"} arXiv:2401.14311
          %p
            For a very gentle introduction to higher category theory, try
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/week73.html#tale"}
                The Tale of
                = succeed "-Categories" do
                  %em n
          %p For a slightly more formal but still pathetically easy introduction, try:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9705009"} An Introduction to n-Categories
          %p
            %em> 7th Conference on Category Theory and Computer Science
            , eds.
          %ul
            %li E. Moggi and G. Rosolini, Springer Lecture Notes in Computer Science vol. 1290, Springer, Berlin, 1997.
          %p
            For a free introductory text on
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %em full of pictures
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugenia+Cheng"} Eugenia Cheng
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Lauda"} Aaron Lauda
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cheng.staff.shef.ac.uk/guidebook/"} Higher-Dimensional Categories: An Illustrated Guidebook
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"} Tom Leinster
            has written about “comparative
            = succeed "-categoriology\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/01/comparative_smootheology.html"} borrow
            a term):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                %em A Survey of Definitions of n-Category
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0107188"}> arXiv
                )
            %li
              %p
                Tom Leinster,
                %em Higher Operads, Higher Categories
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0305049"}> arXiv
                )
          %p A grand picture of the theory of higher categories is drawn in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Simpson"}> Carlos Simpson
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Theory+of+Higher+Categories"} Homotopy Theory of Higher Categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/docs/00/44/98/26/PDF/main.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Another collection of discussions of definitions of higher categories is given at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Approaching+Higher+Category+Theory"} Approaching Higher Category Theory
          %p A brief useful survey of approaches to the definition of higher categories is provided by the set of slides
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Joyal"}> Andre Joyal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              %em Weak categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://web.archive.org/web/20150326110254/http://www.ima.umn.edu/talks/workshops/SP6.7-18.04/may/PorterMay.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            has reached a point where it is well developed and being applied to a wealth of problems with
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0608040"}> arXiv
              )
          %p There’s a lot more to add here, even if we restrict ourselves to very general texts. (More specialized stuff should go under more specialized subcategories!)
